<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal making good EMU progress - Tietmeyer.</title>
<headline>Portugal making good EMU progress - Tietmeyer.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal is making good progress towards fulfilling the criteria for entry to the European Union's Economic and Monetary Union (EMU), Bundesbank chairman Hans Tietmeyer said.</p>
<p>&quot;The country is doing a good job. I hope it makes it (qualifies),&quot; he told journalists after meeting Prime Minister Antonio Guterres.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer is in Portugal, which has made qualifying for EMU its top policy priority, to attend celebrations marking the 150th anniversary of the Bank of Portugal.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
